<title>PERU: Peru's Tele 2000 mulls details of capital increase.</title>
<headline>Peru's Tele 2000 mulls details of capital increase.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peruvian telecom Tele 2000 -- controlled by the United States' BellSouth Corp -- will discuss Friday plans to increase its capital by $50 million, the Lima Stock Exchange said Thursday.</p>
<p>Tele 2000, which announced the planned increase in April, hopes to decide Friday how to obtain the new capital, the exchange said in its daily report.</p>
<p>Tele 2000 is the country's second largest telecommunications firm, providing cellular telephone and cable television services.</p>
<p>((-- Marco Aquino, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
</text>
